── detail · found in your environment ──
radar found a Slack user token in your environment. Do you want to use it?

FOUND
SLACK_APP_USER_OAUTH_TOKEN  the token (xoxp-…)

radar stores only the variables' names (env:NAME) and reads their values each time it starts. It never shows the values or saves them.

IF YOU USE IT
radar sets the token to env:SLACK_APP_USER_OAUTH_TOKEN and checks it with Slack.

⏎ uses it

§ :connection: MAKE A USER TOKEN  about two minutes, once
  1 Open Slack's new-app page, radar's manifest filled in:
  api.slack.com / new app   open · copy manifest
  user scopes only: 10
  2 Pick your workspace, Next, Create.
  3 Install to Workspace, then Allow.
  4 OAuth & Permissions shows the User OAuth Token, xoxp-…: paste it into token, or:
  $ export SLACK_TOKEN=xoxp-…
  then the token is env:SLACK_TOKEN
  api.slack.com / your apps
§ :team: NEEDS AN ADMIN?
  If Slack says Request to Install, your admin approves it first.
  A missing scope switches off only its own actions.
§ :link: MORE
  Slack: what each scope allows
